 "summary": "The XML-based interchange format for Petri nets standardised as ISO/IEC 15909-2: a core model of nets, pages, places, transitions and arcs with labels, specialised by Petri Net Type Definitions (PNTDs) for place/transition nets, symmetric nets and high-level Petri nets with many-sorted algebraic annotations.",
 "status": "maintained",
 "defined_by": [
  "international-standard",
  "academic-paper"
 ],
 "file_extensions": [
  ".pnml"
 ],
 "homepage": "https://www.pnml.org/",
 "level_notes": {
  "1": "ISO/IEC 15909-2:2011 is paywalled; the RELAX NG grammars and Schematron constraints published on pnml.org are the free normative artefacts, alongside Kindler/Hillah papers.",
  "0": "PNML Framework (LIP6) is the reference Java implementation; Model Checking Contest tools consume PNML."
 },
